{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","level":2,"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" macro generates a separate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" class for each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":" property. A view reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.items","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" won’t re-render when only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" macro generates the observer class tree and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading","anchor":"Effect-Threading"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"text":", async file I\/O instead of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadat